## Upgrading from SDKv2

This resource uses Plugin Framework. Existing resource addresses and
`namespace/name` IDs are unchanged; upgrading `kubernetes_pod_v1` does not require
renaming the resource, a `moved` block, or re-import.

The `resources` configuration inside both `container` and `init_container` now
uses list assignment (`resources = [{ ... }]`) instead of a `resources` block.
The `spec.image_pull_secrets` and `spec.readiness_gate` fields also use list
assignments instead of blocks.
Newly created Pods retain configured quantity spelling rather than
being normalized to the API's spelling; equivalent allocations are unchanged.
See the [Pod migration guide](../guides/pod-v1-framework-migration.md) for before
and after examples, dynamic blocks, and moves from the deprecated `kubernetes_pod`
resource. Review the upgrade plan before applying; the syntax change alone must
not replace a Pod.

